</li>
<li data-start="2343" data-end="2709">
<p data-start="2345" data-end="2709"><strong data-start="2345" data-end="2387">Phyllotaxis / Vogel spiral literature.</strong> The golden-angle increment is known to produce <strong data-start="2435" data-end="2461">balanced, low-clumping</strong> angular distributions in spiral packing models (Vogel spiral, phyllotaxis), used in physics/communications for uniformity in the disk/sphere. This gives prior art for the <strong data-start="2633" data-end="2660">self-balancing coverage</strong> intuition. <span class="" data-state="closed"><span class="ms-1 inline-flex max-w-full items-center relative top-[-0.094rem] animate-[show_150ms_ease-in]" data-testid="webpage-citation-pill"><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1345713/?utm_source=chatgpt.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1345713/?utm_source=chatgpt.com" class="flex h-4.5 overflow-hidden rounded-xl px-2 text-[9px] font-medium transition-colors duration-150 ease-in-out text-token-text-secondary! bg-[#F4F4F4]! dark:bg-[#303030]!"><span class="relative start-0 bottom-0 flex h-full w-full items-center"><span class="flex h-4 w-full items-center justify-between absolute" style="opacity: 0; transform: none;"><span class="max-w-[15ch] grow truncate overflow-hidden text-center">Physical Review Links</span><span class="-me-1 flex h-full items-center rounded-full px-1 text-[#8F8F8F]">+3</span></span><span class="flex h-4 w-full items-center justify-between" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><span class="max-w-[15ch] grow truncate overflow-hidden text-center">PMC</span><span class="-me-1 flex h-full items-center rounded-full px-1 text-[#8F8F8F]">+3</span></span><span class="flex h-4 w-full items-center justify-between absolute" style="opacity: 0; transform: translateX(10%);"><span class="max-w-[15ch] grow truncate overflow-hidden text-center">arXiv</span><span class="-me-1 flex h-full items-center rounded-full px-1 text-[#8F8F8F]">+3</span></span></span></a></span></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<blockquote data-start="2711" data-end="2919">
<p data-start="2713" data-end="2919">We <strong data-start="2716" data-end="2726">do not</strong> claim optimality from these facts; we claim that the <strong data-start="2780" data-end="2803">directional targets</strong> are evenly spread, which the greedy selector then tries to match with available points, minimizing <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</blockquote>
