<h2 data-start="3906" data-end="3949">4. Claims, Lemmas &amp; Where We’re Cautious</h2>
<h3 data-start="3951" data-end="4000">4.1 “Near-zero crossings” — careful statement</h3>
<ul data-start="4001" data-end="5089">
<li data-start="4001" data-end="4209">
<p data-start="4003" data-end="4209"><strong data-start="4003" data-end="4027">Theorem (classical):</strong> Any optimal Euclidean TSP tour is crossing-free; if a tour has a crossing, a 2-opt swap strictly reduces length (triangle inequality argument). <span class="" data-state="closed"><span class="ms-1 inline-flex max-w-full items-center relative top-[-0.094rem] animate-[show_150ms_ease-in]" data-testid="webpage-citation-pill"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Travelling_salesman_problem?utm_source=chatgpt.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Travelling_salesman_problem?utm_source=chatgpt.com" class="flex h-4.5 overflow-hidden rounded-xl px-2 text-[9px] font-medium transition-colors duration-150 ease-in-out text-token-text-secondary! bg-[#F4F4F4]! dark:bg-[#303030]!"><span class="relative start-0 bottom-0 flex h-full w-full items-center"><span class="flex h-4 w-full items-center justify-between" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><span class="max-w-[15ch] grow truncate overflow-hidden text-center">Wikipedia</span><span class="-me-1 flex h-full items-center rounded-full px-1 text-[#8F8F8F]">+1</span></span></span></a></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="4210" data-end="4808">
<p data-start="4212" data-end="4808"><strong data-start="4212" data-end="4237">Lemma (GAO tendency):</strong> If successive steps follow increasing polar angle (within a small angular tolerance) and radial changes are small, the immediate edges tend to be <strong data-start="4384" data-end="4405">radially monotone</strong> and <strong data-start="4410" data-end="4441">respect local angular order</strong>, which <strong data-start="4449" data-end="4490">reduces the opportunity for crossings</strong> versus distance-only greedy choices.<br data-start="4527" data-end="4530">
<em data-start="4532" data-end="4541">Sketch:</em> edges that connect neighbors in angular order with modest radial drift are less likely to “jump across” other edges than nearest-neighbor steps that frequently backtrack over large angular gaps. (We propose this as a <strong data-start="4759" data-end="4786">mechanistic explanation</strong>, not a formal bound.)</p>
</li>
<li data-start="4809" data-end="5089">
<p data-start="4811" data-end="5089"><strong data-start="4811" data-end="4839">Empirical Hypothesis H1:</strong> GAO constructs tours with <strong data-start="4866" data-end="4904">significantly fewer edge crossings</strong> than Nearest Neighbor and standard Sweep-then-connect baselines <strong data-start="4969" data-end="4979">before</strong> any 2-opt (Sec. 8).<br data-start="4999" data-end="5002">
<em data-start="5004" data-end="5011">Note:</em> This is explicitly <strong data-start="5031" data-end="5044">empirical</strong>; we do <strong data-start="5052" data-end="5059">not</strong> claim a worst-case guarantee.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="5091" data-end="5157">4.2 “Uniform spatial coverage” — what we prove vs. hypothesize</h3>
<ul data-start="5158" data-end="5558">
<li data-start="5158" data-end="5258">
<p data-start="5160" data-end="5258"><strong data-start="5160" data-end="5169">Fact:</strong> <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha_t\}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mopen">{</span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0037em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class="mclose">}</span></span></span></span> are equidistributed (Sec. 2.2). <span class="" data-state="closed"><span class="ms-1 inline-flex max-w-full items-center relative top-[-0.094rem] animate-[show_150ms_ease-in]" data-testid="webpage-citation-pill"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equidistribution_theorem?utm_source=chatgpt.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equidistribution_theorem?utm_source=chatgpt.com" class="flex h-4.5 overflow-hidden rounded-xl px-2 text-[9px] font-medium transition-colors duration-150 ease-in-out text-token-text-secondary! bg-[#F4F4F4]! dark:bg-[#303030]!"><span class="relative start-0 bottom-0 flex h-full w-full items-center"><span class="flex h-4 w-full items-center justify-between overflow-hidden" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><span class="max-w-[15ch] grow truncate overflow-hidden text-center">Wikipedia</span></span></span></a></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="5259" data-end="5558">
<p data-start="5261" data-end="5558"><strong data-start="5261" data-end="5279">Hypothesis H2:</strong> When point density is not extremely anisotropic, minimizing <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="script">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathcal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">D</span></span></span></span> at each step approximates mapping many <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_t</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.5806em; vertical-align: -0.15em;"></span><span class="mord"><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span><span class="msupsub"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.2806em;"><span style="top: -2.55em; margin-left: -0.0037em; margin-right: 0.05em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 2.7em;"></span><span class="sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight"><span class="mord mathnormal mtight">t</span></span></span></span><span class="vlist-s">​</span></span><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.15em;"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> to nearby unvisited points, inducing <strong data-start="5445" data-end="5474">balanced angular coverage</strong> over time (supported by phyllotaxis analogs). <span class="" data-state="closed"><span class="ms-1 inline-flex max-w-full items-center relative top-[-0.094rem] animate-[show_150ms_ease-in]" data-testid="webpage-citation-pill"><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1345713/?utm_source=chatgpt.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1345713/?utm_source=chatgpt.com" class="flex h-4.5 overflow-hidden rounded-xl px-2 text-[9px] font-medium transition-colors duration-150 ease-in-out text-token-text-secondary! bg-[#F4F4F4]! dark:bg-[#303030]!"><span class="relative start-0 bottom-0 flex h-full w-full items-center"><span class="flex h-4 w-full items-center justify-between overflow-hidden" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><span class="max-w-[15ch] grow truncate overflow-hidden text-center">PMC</span></span></span></a></span></span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start="5560" data-end="5597">4.3 “Fast refinement convergence”</h3>
<ul data-start="5598" data-end="6097">
<li data-start="5598" data-end="5874">
<p data-start="5600" data-end="5874"><strong data-start="5600" data-end="5609">Fact:</strong> Any crossing can be removed by a 2-opt that shortens the tour; fewer crossings generally mean <strong data-start="5704" data-end="5736">fewer profitable 2-opt moves</strong> needed to reach a 2-opt local minimum. This relationship is standard in analyses of 2-opt dynamics. <span class="" data-state="closed"><span class="ms-1 inline-flex max-w-full items-center relative top-[-0.094rem] animate-[show_150ms_ease-in]" data-testid="webpage-citation-pill"><a href="https://www.roeglin.org/publications/SODA07.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" alt="https://www.roeglin.org/publications/SODA07.pdf?utm_source=chatgpt.com" class="flex h-4.5 overflow-hidden rounded-xl px-2 text-[9px] font-medium transition-colors duration-150 ease-in-out text-token-text-secondary! bg-[#F4F4F4]! dark:bg-[#303030]!"><span class="relative start-0 bottom-0 flex h-full w-full items-center"><span class="flex h-4 w-full items-center justify-between" style="opacity: 1; transform: none;"><span class="max-w-[15ch] grow truncate overflow-hidden text-center">roeglin.org</span><span class="-me-1 flex h-full items-center rounded-full px-1 text-[#8F8F8F]">+1</span></span></span></a></span></span></p>
</li>
<li data-start="5875" data-end="6097">
<p data-start="5877" data-end="6097"><strong data-start="5877" data-end="5895">Hypothesis H3:</strong> Since GAO reduces initial crossings (H1), <strong data-start="5938" data-end="5959">2-opt convergence</strong> (number of improving moves) is faster than from NN/Sweep initializations on typical Euclidean instances (Sec. 8). (We will measure this.)</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start="6099" data-end="6198">We mark H1–H3 as <strong data-start="6116" data-end="6130">hypotheses</strong> backed by mechanism + references, and we validate them empirically.</p>
<hr data-start="6200" data-end="6203">
<h2 data-start="6205" data-end="6238">5. Complexity (with reasoning)</h2>
<ol data-start="6240" data-end="7132">
<li data-start="6240" data-end="6303">
<p data-start="6243" data-end="6303"><strong data-start="6243" data-end="6261">Preprocessing:</strong> centroid + polar transform in <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6304" data-end="6444">
<p data-start="6307" data-end="6444"><strong data-start="6307" data-end="6328">Angular indexing:</strong> build <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span></span></span></span> bins by <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span></span></span></span> in <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> (or sort by <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6944em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">θ</span></span></span></span> in <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n\log n)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mop">lo<span style="margin-right: 0.01389em;">g</span></span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.1667em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> if you prefer; either works).</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6445" data-end="7132">
<p data-start="6448" data-end="6479"><strong data-start="6448" data-end="6477">Main loop (n iterations):</strong></p>
<ul data-start="6483" data-end="7132">
<li data-start="6483" data-end="6521">
<p data-start="6485" data-end="6521">Compute next <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span></span></span></span>: <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord">1</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="6525" data-end="6810">
<p data-start="6527" data-end="6810"><strong data-start="6527" data-end="6551">Candidate retrieval:</strong> probe the bin nearest <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.4306em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.0037em;">α</span></span></span></span>; expected constant work if bins are balanced. In adversarial cases, probing up to <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(B)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.02778em;">O</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span><span class="mclose">)</span></span></span></span> bins is possible, but with <span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>n</mi></msqrt><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\Theta(\sqrt{n})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right: 0.05017em;">B</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span><span class="mrel">=</span><span class="mspace" style="margin-right: 0.2778em;"></span></span><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height: 1.0503em; vertical-align: -0.25em;"></span><span class="mord">Θ</span><span class="mopen">(</span><span class="mord sqrt"><span class="vlist-t vlist-t2"><span class="vlist-r"><span class="vlist" style="height: 0.8003em;"><span class="svg-align" style="top: -3em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="mord" style="padding-left: 0.833em;"><span class="mord mathnormal">n</span></span></span><span style="top: -2.7603em;"><span class="pstrut" style="height: 3em;"></span><span class="hide-tail" style="min-width: 0.853em; height: 1.08em;"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="400em" height="1.08em" viewBox="0 0 400000 1080" preserveAspectRatio="xMinYMin slice"><path d="M95,702
