MIT-licensed reference implementation accompanying the paper:

</span><span><span class="hljs-quote">&gt; <span class="hljs-strong">**“The Golden-Angle Greedy Algorithm for the Euclidean Travelling Salesman Problem (GAO Spiral)” (2025)**</span></span></span><span>

---

</span><span><span class="hljs-section">## 🌻 Overview</span></span><span>
GAO Spiral is a </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**directional greedy heuristic**</span></span><span> for the Euclidean Travelling Salesman Problem (TSP).
Instead of choosing the </span><span><span class="hljs-emphasis">*nearest*</span></span><span> next point (as in Nearest Neighbor), GAO Spiral chooses the point </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**nearest along a rotating golden-angle direction**</span></span><span>—a rule that balances local greediness with global spatial coherence.

</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Input:**</span></span><span> 2D coordinates of </span><span><span class="hljs-code">`n`</span></span><span> points
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Output:**</span></span><span> One TSP tour (a sequence visiting each point exactly once)
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Complexity:**</span></span><span> O(n log n) expected
</span><span><span class="hljs-bullet">-</span></span><span> </span><span><span class="hljs-strong">**Core idea:**</span></span><span> “Greedy without chaos”—each step greedily reduces angular disorder, following the golden-angle rotation (≈137.5°).

---

