<h3 data-start="1599" data-end="1608">⚡Tips</h3>
<ul data-start="1609" data-end="1905">
<li data-start="1609" data-end="1761">
<p data-start="1611" data-end="1761">You can safely parallelize per seed or dataset (the code is embarrassingly parallel) using <code data-start="1702" data-end="1719">multiprocessing</code> if you want to cut that to ~30 s total.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1762" data-end="1832">
<p data-start="1764" data-end="1832">If you bump the 2-opt budget to 10 000, expect roughly ×3 runtime.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="1833" data-end="1905">
<p data-start="1835" data-end="1905">For large paper-scale runs (n = 5 000+), expect minutes per algorithm.</p>
</li>
</ul>
