<div class="_tableContainer_1rjym_1"><div tabindex="-1" class="group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse"><table data-start="457" data-end="1692" class="w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)"><thead data-start="457" data-end="508"><tr data-start="457" data-end="508"><th data-start="457" data-end="461" data-col-size="sm">#</th><th data-start="461" data-end="469" data-col-size="md">Check</th><th data-start="469" data-end="486" data-col-size="sm">Why it matters</th><th data-start="486" data-end="508" data-col-size="md">Simple Python test</th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="561" data-end="1692"><tr data-start="561" data-end="670"><td data-start="561" data-end="569" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="563" data-end="568">1</strong></td><td data-start="569" data-end="624" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="571" data-end="588">Tour validity</strong> — each vertex visited exactly once</td><td data-start="624" data-end="645" data-col-size="sm">Core TSP invariant</td><td data-start="645" data-end="670" data-col-size="md"><code data-start="647" data-end="668">len(set(tour)) == n</code></td></tr><tr data-start="671" data-end="831"><td data-start="671" data-end="679" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="673" data-end="678">2</strong></td><td data-start="679" data-end="746" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="681" data-end="707">Closed loop continuity</strong> — start/end distance non-pathological</td><td data-start="746" data-end="772" data-col-size="sm">Detects broken end join</td><td data-start="772" data-end="831" data-col-size="md">Compare <code data-start="782" data-end="807">dist(tour[0], tour[-1])</code> to median edge length</td></tr><tr data-start="832" data-end="932"><td data-start="832" data-end="840" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="834" data-end="839">3</strong></td><td data-start="840" data-end="871" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="842" data-end="870">Edge length distribution</strong></td><td data-start="871" data-end="898" data-col-size="sm">Reveals jumps/backtracks</td><td data-start="898" data-end="932" data-col-size="md">Plot histogram of edge lengths</td></tr><tr data-start="933" data-end="1075"><td data-start="933" data-end="941" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="935" data-end="940">4</strong></td><td data-start="941" data-end="980" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="943" data-end="979">Angular progression monotonicity</strong></td><td data-start="980" data-end="1008" data-col-size="sm">Confirms “spiral” pattern</td><td data-start="1008" data-end="1075" data-col-size="md">Compute Δθ sequence of edges, check if roughly uniform rotation</td></tr><tr data-start="1076" data-end="1183"><td data-start="1076" data-end="1084" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1078" data-end="1083">5</strong></td><td data-start="1084" data-end="1110" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="1086" data-end="1109">Radial monotonicity</strong></td><td data-start="1110" data-end="1153" data-col-size="sm">Ensures outward/inward wave, not erratic</td><td data-start="1153" data-end="1183" data-col-size="md">Plot r[i] along tour index</td></tr><tr data-start="1184" data-end="1306"><td data-start="1184" data-end="1192" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1186" data-end="1191">6</strong></td><td data-start="1192" data-end="1214" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="1194" data-end="1213">Crossing sanity</strong></td><td data-start="1214" data-end="1243" data-col-size="sm">Detects geometric tangling</td><td data-start="1243" data-end="1306" data-col-size="md">Count crossings (should scale near-linearly with n, not n²)</td></tr><tr data-start="1307" data-end="1422"><td data-start="1307" data-end="1315" data-col-size="sm"><strong data-start="1309" data-end="1314">7</strong></td><td data-start="1315" data-end="1351" data-col-size="md"><strong data-start="1317" data-end="1350">Determinism / seed invariance</strong></td><td data-start="1351" data-end="1377" data-col-size="sm">Confirm reproducibility</td><td