<h2 data-start="2981" data-end="3043">D) 2D binning (θ × r) for finer <strong data-start="3016" data-end="3027">Textura</strong> + <strong data-start="3030" data-end="3043">Adaptatio</strong></h2>
<p data-start="3044" data-end="3211"><strong data-start="3044" data-end="3053">Idea:</strong> index by angle <strong data-start="3069" data-end="3076">and</strong> coarse radius band, not just angle.<br data-start="3112" data-end="3115">
<strong data-start="3115" data-end="3123">Why:</strong> ensures candidates are already radius-compatible → smoother |Δr| and more even texture.</p>
<p data-start="3213" data-end="3235">Implementation sketch:</p>
<ul data-start="3236" data-end="3423">
<li data-start="3236" data-end="3279">
<p data-start="3238" data-end="3279">Choose <code data-start="3245" data-end="3260">Bθ = int(2√n)</code>, <code data-start="3262" data-end="3278">Br = int(√n/4)</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3280" data-end="3334">
<p data-start="3282" data-end="3334">Put each point in bin <code data-start="3304" data-end="3333">(⌊θ/(2π)·Bθ⌋, ⌊r/r_max·Br⌋)</code>.</p>
</li>
<li data-start="3335" data-end="3423">
<p data-start="3337" data-end="3423">When targeting <code data-start="3352" data-end="3359">alpha</code>, probe angle bin(s) near it <strong data-start="3388" data-end="3395">and</strong> the current radius band ±1.</p>
</li>
</ul>
